      "content": "Yes, subconsciously, the presentation suggests a difference in perceived status that a reviewer might lean into. Dr. Sterling's name and the high-tech nature of his study lend an aura of established, high-tier institutional authority. Conversely, Dr. Adeyemi's approach, while valuable, might be subtly perceived as more localized or preliminary background research, reflecting current trends in diverse scholarship. This subtle framing can lead reviewers to apply a higher initial weight to Sterling's claimed \"framework.\"",
